{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>When you build a new house.</b> If you have fulfilled the commandment of sending the nest, you will eventually build a new house and fulfill the commandment of the parapet — for a commandment draws after it a commandment — and you will arrive at a vineyard and a field and fine garments. Therefore these passages are juxtaposed (Tanḥuma)." "<b>Parapet.</b> A fence around the roof. And Onkelos renders it ״תְּיָקָא״ — like a case (תִּיק) that protects what is inside it." "<b>That the faller fall.</b> This one was fit to fall; even so, his death shall not come about through you — for merit is drawn through the hand of the meritorious, and liability through the hand of the liable (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:59.535610831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}